Diagnosis: why does primary ONMI RISE with blend_strength (real overlap signal)?
n_nodes=300, k=5, 5 seeds, NF-MCD default. Conditions: combined (edges+content blended,
matches run_overlap2.py), edge_only, content_only (ablation; blend=0 has only 'combined',
identical to both ablations trivially).
====================================================================================================


### Mechanism 2 (scoring/credit) + Mechanism 3 (structural spillover): 'combined' condition
strict_acc = hard assignment must map to the NOMINAL primary community c1.
lenient_acc = hard assignment may map to EITHER true community (c1 or c2) -- this is what
the standard overlapping_nmi metric effectively rewards for overlapping nodes.
====================================================================================================

